---
layout: base.njk
wide: true
pagination:
  data: collections.shelves
  size: 1
  alias: shelf
permalink: "/shelf/{{ shelf.category }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ shelf.label }}"
---
{% set items = collections.subjectPages | inCategory(shelf.category) | shelveSort %}

<h1>{{ shelf.label }}</h1>

{#- Two jobs, split across two pieces of art. The COVER identifies: a reader
    hunting for one game scans box art far faster than titles, and faster still
    than a dozen abstract night scenes that deliberately encode no identity.
    The BANNER above it is that subject's own sky cropped to a strip, and it
    keeps both axes the tile always carried — how much aurora is left says
    status, how brightly it burns says how recently it was written about. The
    shelf still reads as a state-of-the-category at a glance; you just no longer
    have to decode which scene is which game to use it.

    Covers are SOURCED, and sourced means sometimes absent. A subject without
    one falls back to the whole generated tile, stretched by CSS to the exact
    height the banner-and-cover stack comes to — so the original guarantee holds
    (no shelf goes blank waiting on an image) and a half-covered shelf still
    lays out as one even grid rather than a ragged one. -#}
<ul class="shelf-grid">
  {% for item in items %}
  <li class="shelf-item">
    <a href="/s/{{ item.slug }}/">
      <span class="shelf-art">
        {% if item.coverUrl %}
        <span class="sky sky-banner" style="background-image:url({{ item.bannerUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {#- A real <img>, unlike every sky on the site: the generated art is
            decoration and belongs in CSS, but a cover is content, it wants an
            alt, and a shelf that keeps growing wants lazy loading. -#}
        <img class="shelf-cover" src="{{ item.coverUrl }}" alt="{{ item.title }} cover art" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        {% else %}
        <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ item.skyUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {% endif %}
      </span>
      <span class="shelf-caption">{{ item.title }}</span>
      <span class="badge b-{{ item.status }}">{{ item.status }}</span>
      {% if item.rating %}<span class="rating">{{ item.rating }}/5</span>{% endif %}
    </a>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
